  "body": "# Backend\r\npython - REST api based on [klein](https://github.com/twisted/klein) which produces the configs\r\nby templating the sample config generated by synapse.\r\n\r\n# Frontend\r\nReact-Redux, es6 and a bunch of other goodies\r\n\r\n# It's a setup util\r\nThis util is just a very simple initial setup thing. It will walk users through picking a username and setting up ports. It will handhold users looking to use a reverse proxy and delegation. Once it's at this point I would be very happy with the project. There's still plenty of scope for it to become the defacto config util for synapse but that may be for later.\r\n\r\n# Federation tester:\r\nIt will include some simple utils to test the setup.\r\n\r\n# Config editor\r\nWe've decided not to allow editing of the yaml files inside the installer.\r\n# Milestones:\r\n\r\n- [x] servername setup \r\n- [x] Ask for consent to send usage stats to matrix.org\r\n- [x] Delegation options\r\n- [x] Reverse Proxy options\r\n- [x] Tls / ACME\r\n- [x] Port configuration\r\n- [x] Template output\r\n- [ ] Database configuration\r\n- [x] YAML dumper\r\n- [ ] Federation testing\r\n- [x] back button\r\n\r\noptimisation / env settings\r\n\r\n# Other things to think about\r\n- LDAP\r\n- TURN\r\n- Consent tracking\r\n- Admin user\r\n- Email settings\r\n- Advanced listener support\r\n- User related settings\r\n- search related settings\r\n- manhole\r\n- security settings\r\n- advanced settings\r\n\r\n",
